  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">You are well-versed in how to treat the ill and dying, but this gives you the right knowledge on how to make injuries worse. When you Strike a creature with a slashing or piercing weapon or cast a spell that deals slashing or piercing damage against a creature suffering from persistent bleed or poison damage, you can rupture their injury or a regulating organ. The target gains weakness 5 to bleed or poison for 1 round, depending on which persistent damage they are suffering from. This weakness is doubled on a critical hit. At a GM’s discretion, a creature afflicted with a poison that deals poison damage can also qualify for Rupturing Touch.</span></p>"
